  "articleBody": "Getting arrested by federal agents can feel overwhelming and confusing, right? It's a different ballgame than state charges, and knowing what to expect can help you prepare. Your journey usually starts with an arrest, often by agencies like the FBI, DEA, or IRS, followed by booking and an initial appearance before a federal magistrate judge. This first hearing is super important; it's where bail conditions might be set, or you might be detained. Next up is the indictment, where a grand jury decides if there's enough evidence to formally charge you. If indicted, you'll have an arraignment to enter your plea. Discovery then kicks off, and both sides exchange evidence. Pre-trial motions come next, where your attorney can challenge evidence or procedures. If a plea agreement isn't reached, you're headed for trial. The federal system has strict rules and high stakes, so having an experienced attorney on your side, like Angelo Reyes, who understands these specific processes, is critical from the very beginning. They can help protect your rights every step of the way.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
}